Cell["Part II. Exact common variables and the two limits", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"de5c06d3-9db2-485d-b959-b81ecc70be8a"],

Cell["7. Exact variables before either limit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"db32e6f0-82b3-4b22-aa3d-024230e40a7c"],

Cell["\<\
For comparing with the central-soft MRK analysis, introduce the exact \
transverse ratios and longitudinal ratios in the (p1,p2) light-cone frame:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46d51d9f-4204-419a-a9ca-dfcb1318eb08"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"variable\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"exact definition\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"w", "\<\"-p3_perp/p4_perp\"\>"},
    {"\<\"wbar\"\>", "\<\"-p3bar_perp/p4bar_perp\"\>"},
    {"\<\"zeta=-1/w\"\>", "\<\"p4_perp/p3_perp\"\>"},
    {"\<\"zetabar=-1/wbar\"\>", "\<\"p4bar_perp/p3bar_perp\"\>"},
    {"X34", "\<\"p3+/p4+\"\>"},
    {"X45", "\<\"p4+/p5+\"\>"},
    {
     SubsuperscriptBox["Q", "4", "2"], "\<\"|p4_perp|^2 (overall scale)\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"87748018-1278-4c5f-893f-98d881470e73"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"w", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       FractionBox["p3perp", "p4perp"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"wb", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       FractionBox["p3barperp", "p4barperp"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"zeta", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       FractionBox["1", "w"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"zetab", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       FractionBox["1", "wb"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"X34", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["p3plus", "p4plus"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"X45", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["p4plus", "p5plus"]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"1ad1cdcc-b6b4-4fa6-b1be-\
ca424aafda2d"],

Cell["\<\
These four ratios together with |p4_perp|^2 provide a convenient exact chart. \
They are introduced only after the invariant construction, so the existence \
of the near-planar region does not depend on this choice. In the convention \
of the five-point MRK paper q2_perp=p3_perp, not p4_perp, and therefore\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4bd0d649-4371-4309-aec1-fe87b2e7f39e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     TemplateBox[{"q2perp"},
      "Abs"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"w", " ", "wb", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
       "Abs"], "2"]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"a8986f0d-e60a-4621-b4de-\
7d0d80c396e1"],

Cell["\<\
Up to the fixed orientation convention for epsilon5, the parity-odd invariant \
has the exact factorized form\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cc9a45d-b53e-4b56-a24c-c2ceb5c41eea"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"epsilon5", "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"s12", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
       "Abs"], "2"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"w", "-", "wb"}], ")"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"s12", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
        "Abs"], "2"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"zeta", "-", "zetab"}], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"zeta", " ", "zetab"}]]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"07b562f7-596c-4bf1-978b-\
05e6b010cd8d"],

Cell["\<\
This is the generic five-point chart before either expansion is taken. The \
two limits below are independent paths from this same domain. Near-planar \
wide angle sends the angular difference zeta-zetabar to zero at fixed \
|p4_perp|^2. Central-soft MRK instead sends |p4_perp|^2 to zero while \
zeta/zetabar remains generic. It is not obtained by first imposing \
coplanarity and then taking a soft MRK sublimit.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d27e5e99-eb3b-40aa-8dad-44e72a40ce86"],

Cell["7.1 Symmetric variables for physical interpretation", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fd4dc4c9-dc38-4fdb-bd1c-654286b65339"],

Cell["\<\
The exact X variables use plus components on both sides of the central \
emission. This is algebraically convenient but not symmetric under exchanging \
the forward and backward rapidity sectors. Introduce instead\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f4ecb681-de69-4b82-b1a6-95aa53a1ccdc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"R34", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"X34", " ", 
        TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
         "Abs"]}], 
       TemplateBox[{"p3perp"},
        "Abs"]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"R45", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"X45", " ", 
        TemplateBox[{"p5perp"},
         "Abs"]}], 
       TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
        "Abs"]]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"cd1b054c-ecfc-4c13-9a93-\
4d9f2ba426ea"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"R34", "\[LongEqual]", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"y3", "-", "y4"}]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"R45", "\[LongEqual]", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{"y4", "-", "y5"}]]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"a7fe7e5a-e6e0-41c4-bb03-\
b5ba2d594712"],

Cell["\<\
These quantities measure only the two rapidity gaps. The independent variable \
kappa=|p4_perp|/Q_perp measures the softness of the central emission. If a \
rational parametrization is required, use the squares\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05fa06fc-f3b6-431e-93e4-ca3b017e323e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["R34", "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["X34", "2"], " ", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
          "Abs"], "2"]}], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        TemplateBox[{"p3perp"},
         "Abs"], "2"]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["R45", "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["X45", "2"], " ", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         TemplateBox[{"p5perp"},
          "Abs"], "2"]}], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
         "Abs"], "2"]]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b4b0704a-0f91-46e1-8659-\
cbb36864aef5"],

Cell["8. Angular near-planar wide-angle limit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0bc2f246-74f7-42fa-9d21-db4c35ab8b35"],

Cell["\<\
Keep |p4_perp|^2, X34, X45 and the remaining wide-angle ratios finite. The \
physical approach from one orientation is\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4e18b841-df96-46fe-85ec-97bed2e0c3f2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"w", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        FractionBox["1", "xi"]}], "+", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "\[Lambda]"}], "2"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"wb", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        FractionBox["1", "xi"]}], "-", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "\[Lambda]"}], "2"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"zeta", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["xi", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "xi"}], "2"]}]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"zetab", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["xi", 
       RowBox[{"1", "+", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "xi"}], "2"]}]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"xi", ">", "0"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", ">", "0"}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"d7337fa8-1106-4197-ae83-\
e76be475f53b"],

Cell["\<\
Thus zeta and zetabar are complex conjugates in the physical non-coplanar \
region and become equal to the positive real number xi at the coplanar \
boundary. Equivalently w=wbar=-1/xi there. This makes epsilon5=O(i lambda) \
and Gamma5=O(-lambda^2). It is an angular approach to planarity; no rapidity \
hierarchy and no soft external momentum are taken.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2632d9ea-2c3c-403e-b207-75d9a0d385d7"],

Cell["9. Central-soft MRK in the same variables", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8f81e535-f0a3-4f62-9c04-cab2b86101da"],

Cell["\<\
Starting again from the generic chart, let delta be the MRK parameter, with \
p4_perp~delta^a and x_MRK~delta^b for 0<a<b. The following independent \
rate-resolved path is exactly on shell, not merely a list of leading \
valuations:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a4d5270c-55ea-40d0-a798-1b7085436e12"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"zeta", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"zetaHat", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"zetab", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
        "Abs"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"Q4hat2", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "a"}]]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"X34", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"X34hat", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "-", "b"}]]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"X45", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"X45hat", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
         RowBox[{"a", "-", "b"}]]}], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", 
           SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"]}], "+", "1"}], ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"zetaHat", " ", 
           SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"]}], "+", "1"}], ")"}]}]]}]}], "}"}],
   
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"78e38392-f4d2-4a8e-9e10-\
43fb574ac662"],

Cell["\<\
All hatted quantities are fixed and nonzero; in the physical region \
zetaBarHat is the complex conjugate of zetaHat. The denominator in X45 is \
required for exact on-shell equivalence.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b45e0b99-6fe9-4eae-9da6-96f34b27694d"],

Cell["The exact variables then scale as follows:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"563e037b-1292-410b-9fd7-a9d23856c969"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"quantity\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"near-planar wide angle\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"central-soft MRK\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"|p4_perp|^2\"\>", "\<\"fixed\"\>", "\<\"R delta^(2a)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"zeta, zetabar\"\>", "\<\"xi/(1 -/+ i xi lambda/2)\"\>", \
"\<\"delta^a {zetahat, zetabarhat}\"\>"},
    {"\<\"X34\"\>", "\<\"fixed\"\>", "\<\"X34hat delta^(-(a+b))\"\>"},
    {"\<\"X45\"\>", "\<\"fixed\"\>", "\<\"X45hat delta^(a-b)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"MRK gap x\"\>", "\<\"not taken\"\>", "\<\"delta^b, 0<a<b\"\>"},
    {"\<\"|p4_perp|^2 (zeta-zetabar)/(zeta zetabar)\"\>", \
"\<\"O(lambda)\"\>", "\<\"O(delta^a)\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"92790a8a-8805-445e-ab59-12b55e31b2e5"],

Cell["\<\
The visibly different powers of X34 and X45 do not represent asymmetric \
rapidity gaps: each X also contains a different power of the soft transverse \
momentum. In the symmetric variables the two physical gaps and the softness \
separate cleanly:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"793d7fcd-8450-4a53-a0f3-1add4817e279"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"quantity\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"definition\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"central-soft scaling\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"R34", "\<\"X34 |p4_perp|/|p3_perp| = exp(y3-y4)\"\>", "\<\"delta^(-b)\"\
\>"},
    {"R45", "\<\"X45 |p5_perp|/|p4_perp| = exp(y4-y5)\"\>", "\<\"delta^(-b)\"\
\>"},
    {"kappa", "\<\"|p4_perp|/Q_perp\"\>", "\<\"delta^a\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"d1d3e70f-db80-4f82-b3d4-840d8af47fbf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"scalesAs", "(", 
       FractionBox["R34", "R45"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"scalesAs", "(", "kappa", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"scalesAs", "(", "R34", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
       RowBox[{"-", "b"}]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"scalesAs", "(", "R45", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
       RowBox[{"-", "b"}]]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"bb02fa3f-efb6-423c-ab6f-\
1105bb063e0d"],

Cell["\<\
For the representative choice a=1,b=2 the powers of \
(|p4_perp|^2,zeta,X34,X45) are (2,1,-3,-1). The normalized parity-odd \
quantity tends to zero:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01b3f94b-5a35-4897-b457-877ed958ee01"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"scalesAs", "(", 
     FractionBox["epsilon5", "s12"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"scalesAs", "(", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
         "Abs"], "2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"zeta", "-", "zetab"}], ")"}]}], 
      RowBox[{"zeta", " ", "zetab"}]], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"8c23c3b8-3955-4ab4-8a55-\
3b94095b7de6"],

Cell["\<\
The dimensionful epsilon5 itself need not tend to zero because s12 grows in \
MRK. At the central-soft endpoint the transverse transfers obey \
q1_perp=-q2_perp and hence t1=t2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8da047a0-815a-41bb-a5f2-99fa61141b57"],

Cell["9.1 Exact equivalence with the earlier light-cone audit", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"912e46f0-52e4-4c76-94dd-9f3f391b89a2"],

Cell["\<\
The existing all-layer audit used finite coefficients P,K,M,R,T,C. It set\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b6858d55-bc8f-451a-8858-9aa410f54109"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"p3plus", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"P", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
        RowBox[{"-", "b"}]]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"p4plus", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"K", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"p5minus", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"M", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
        RowBox[{"-", "b"}]]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       TemplateBox[{"p3perp"},
        "Abs"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", "T"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       TemplateBox[{"p4perp"},
        "Abs"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"R", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "a"}]]}]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"a1787565-3233-492f-8680-\
a67426d007bf"],

Cell["The two descriptions are exactly the same path under", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6da64068-0195-4c6b-8707-ddd1960d8632"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Q4hat2", "\[LongEqual]", "R"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"X34hat", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["P", "K"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"X45hat", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"K", " ", "M"}], "T"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", "zetaHat"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["R", "T"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", "+", "zetaHat"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"C", " ", "sigma"}], "T"]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"11956528-b548-4fb0-bef0-\
aee04db278c4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"R34", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"P", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
         RowBox[{"-", "b"}]], " ", 
        SqrtBox[
         FractionBox["R", "T"]]}], "K"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"R45", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"K", " ", "M", " ", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
          RowBox[{"-", "b"}]]}], 
        SqrtBox[
         RowBox[{"R", " ", "T"}]]], "+", 
       RowBox[{"subleading", "(", "\[Delta]", ")"}]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"kappa", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "a"], " ", 
       SqrtBox[
        FractionBox["R", "T"]]}]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"1bc18b42-75cc-41e4-bdf6-\
4ce5d4feabe5"],

Cell["\<\
Substitution reproduces all five exact adjacent invariants, including their \
subleading layers. Here Q_perp=|p3_perp| was chosen in kappa. Thus the old \
coefficients do not define a different kinematic limit; they are retained \
only as an executable equivalence and positivity audit.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05b4fa30-72a6-4b89-b687-d738d84384fd"],

Cell["9.2 Full-layer hidden-region certificate", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"280bf921-97ab-4beb-b6d7-0e9077992ed6"],

Cell["\<\
For a=1,b=2 the aligned leading polynomial factorizes and defines a \
two-factor cancellation locus:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a88848a-cf63-41e4-acbc-ad0d08bd6bfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["F", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}], "align"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"Q4hat2", " ", "X45hat", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x2", " ", "X34hat"}], "-", "x3"}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
         RowBox[{"x0", " ", "x5"}]}], ")"}]}], 
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", "zetaHat"}]]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"25597d14-f34b-459b-af75-\
286f80779992"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2", " ", "X34hat"}], "-", "x3"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"x0", " ", "x5"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b65762f7-92cc-49cf-99eb-\
7aff062ca828"],

Cell["\<\
The displayed factor is the coefficient of the delta^(-10) layer after \
asymptotic-order alignment alone. It is not a polynomial assigned only to the \
relative HRF stage. The relative HRF vector is uniform, so it contributes -3 \
to every cubic F term and -2 to every quadratic U term. Consequently\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"74e346cc-68b5-45a2-858f-3efb69db8b55"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"stage\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"leading factor\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"next nonzero F layer\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"leading U\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"absolute layers after alignment vector\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "6"}]},
    {"\<\"contribution of relative uniform HRF vector\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "2"}]},
    {"\<\"composed vector\"\>", 
     RowBox[{"-", "13"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "12"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]},
    {"\<\"after imposing the two-factor locus\"\>", "\<\"promoted to -8\"\>", 
     
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"32eb7b6e-5928-4b53-b962-306b28a8fcab"],

Cell["\<\
The sum of the alignment and HRF vectors is (-4,-4,-1,-4,-4,-4;1). This is \
the HRF region vector in the dimensionless convention where the growing hard \
invariant s12 has been factored out. Adding +4 uniformly would convert back \
to dimensionful Schwinger parameters while s12 itself varies, but that \
non-negative representative is not the infrared region vector and is not used \
for the MoR power count.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"90788af8-5452-4079-82d4-3f000c2864d2"],

Cell["The immediately following aligned F layer contains", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae6a873f-e95a-443a-8e63-dd9521fe9f84"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["F", 
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}], "align"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"Q4hat2", " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}], 
      RowBox[{"zetaBarHat", " ", "zetaHat"}]]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"90384bd2-aa0a-46b7-8aa8-\
b132396db5d8"],

Cell["\<\
On the two-factor locus this remains finite and nonzero. It has weight -8, \
exactly the leading U weight. The cancelled factorized sector is promoted \
from W_SL=-9 to the same W_HR=-8 layer. The resolved augmented support has \
full affine rank, and the current audit therefore accepts the region.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe02b0c5-e55d-4011-8567-7be35d26e165"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"item\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"value\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"alignment vector\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{-3, -3, 0, -3, -3, -3}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"]},
    {"\<\"relative HRF vector\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{-1, -1, -1, -1, -1, -1}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"]},
    {"\<\"hard-scale-normalized total vector\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{-4, -4, -1, -4, -4, -4}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"]},
    {"\<\"physical weights (W_SL,W_HR)\"\>", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{-9, -8}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"]},
    {"\<\"current status\"\>", "\<\"AcceptedLowerFacet\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"4eb42612-5aa0-4e85-a86b-e23b4ed627c9"],

Cell["10. What is common and what is distinct", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e42e1345-052c-4e0d-9810-0b083ac887f8"],

Cell["\<\
The two limits reach the normalized planar hypersurface through different \
factors of the same exact expression. Near-planar wide angle keeps |p4_perp| \
finite and sends zeta-zetabar to zero at zeta=zetabar=xi>0. Central-soft MRK \
sends |p4_perp|,zeta and zetabar to zero together. Both possess an HR, but \
they are not two coordinate descriptions of one region.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b496b182-67cd-429f-a8b7-7349494ec37e"],

Cell["\<\
Their limiting ideals are nevertheless related; this comparison does not \
construct either limit as a sublimit of the other. On the aligned \
central-soft face the two corresponding path ratios coincide, so x1 x4-x0 \
x5=x1 fC-x5 fA. The other central-soft factor X34hat x2-x3 equals X34hat fB \
in the aligned variables. Their product therefore belongs to the limiting \
near-planar ideal generated by fA fB and fB fC; the third product fA fC is \
kinematically suppressed on this MRK face. The region vector \
(-4,-4,-1,-4,-4,-4;1) and momentum scaling remain distinct from the uniform \
near-planar vector (-2,-2,-2,-2,-2,-2;1).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"259f7f9d-9548-4f83-a3cc-f10fd2fa8483"],

Cell["Part III. Momentum-space interpretation and power counting", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"3344c1b3-a160-485b-90ad-9f02e3b86b15"],

Cell["11. Complete edge-flow configuration", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0019ebb1-8050-4475-a8fb-e248be35003f"],

Cell["\<\
Orient qA,qB,qC from the common vertex carrying p3 towards the common vertex \
carrying p4. Momentum conservation gives qA+qB+qC=-p3. Along path A the two \
edge momenta are qA and qA-p1; paths B and C are analogous with p2 and p5. \
All momenta use the all-outgoing convention.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"98bc1a57-c609-43fc-ab4b-35d2fc4cde37"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"edge\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"momentum\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"leading flow\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"virtuality\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"x0", "qA", 
     RowBox[{"p1", " ", "xiA"}], "\<\"O(lambda^2 Q^2)\"\>"},
    {"x1", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "p1"}], "+", "qA"}], 
     RowBox[{"p1", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "+", "xiA"}], 
       ")"}]}], "\<\"O(lambda^2 Q^2)\"\>"},
    {"x2", "qB", 
     RowBox[{"p2", " ", "xiB"}], "\<\"O(lambda^2 Q^2)\"\>"},
    {"x3", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "p2"}], "+", "qB"}], 
     RowBox[{"p2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "+", "xiB"}], 
       ")"}]}], "\<\"O(lambda^2 Q^2)\"\>"},
    {"x4", "qC", 
     RowBox[{"p5", " ", "xiC"}], "\<\"O(lambda^2 Q^2)\"\>"},
    {"x5", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "p5"}], "+", "qC"}], 
     RowBox[{"p5", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "+", "xiC"}], ")"}]}], "\<\"O(lambda^2 Q^2)\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"7b35f6b3-9837-4f58-a55c-6d30d0c79865"],

Cell["\<\
The two independent loop Landau equations say that the weighted momentum \
transported by each path is the same:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b29cc1ec-2adf-40b5-84be-5b7e03e66cf5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"qA", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"x0", "+", "x1"}], ")"}]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"p1", " ", "x1"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"qB", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"x2", "+", "x3"}], ")"}]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"p2", " ", "x3"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"qC", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"x4", "+", "x5"}], ")"}]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"p5", " ", "x5"}]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"f39e8fa1-29f6-4711-abde-\
2ce2d7f60c85"],

Cell["\<\
At a positive Landau point all six propagators are on shell. Each pair \
differs by a massless external momentum, so real first-sheet kinematics makes \
the pair collinear to that external direction. Since p1,p2,p5 are not \
mutually collinear, the common weighted vector above must vanish. The loop \
Landau equations therefore fix\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18b2390b-6419-4d6e-806c-3a05911514d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"qA", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"p1", " ", "xiA"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"qB", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"p2", " ", "xiB"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"qC", "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"p5", " ", "xiC"}]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"fa1f9297-2ecb-450e-a6fe-\
71e730d9e118"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xiA", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"rhoA", "+", "1"}]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"xiB", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"rhoB", "+", "1"}]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"xiC", "\[LongEqual]", 
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"rhoC", "+", "1"}]]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"88d1b4ba-c2b9-48e2-8768-\
2c35e17f0d88"],

Cell["\<\
The hard-vertex equation xiA p1+xiB p2+xiC p5=-p3 is soluble precisely on the \
Gram surface Gamma5=0. This is the momentum-space reason the region \
disappears at a generic non-coplanar wide-angle point. At the invariant \
witness used above the fractions are (xiA,xiB,xiC)=(1/5,1/2,1/3).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5939ff1c-c115-493e-90c3-59e45801ce2b"],

Cell["11.1 Modes and restricted longitudinal support", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"21d93101-80ee-42e4-9820-e51c1a53363f"],

Cell["\<\
For each path introduce light-cone vectors v_i and bar(v)_i along and \
opposite to its external direction, an in-plane transverse direction u_i, and \
D-3 transverse directions orthogonal to the scattering plane. Near the pinch,\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f55291a9-ed97-4931-8d2d-c4d82a0add9b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"q", "(", "i", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"Q", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "2"], " ", 
        RowBox[{"barv", "(", "i", ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"kappa", "(", "i", ")"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"boldv", "(", "i", ")"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"tau", "(", "i", ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"u", "(", "i", ")"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"v", "(", "i", ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"xi", "(", "i", ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"85b2b858-492c-440e-ac50-\
768e0db956a2"],

Cell["\<\
so q_i^2 and (q_i-p_i)^2 are both O(lambda^2 Q^2). Only two loop momenta are \
independent; take qA and qB, with qC=-p3-qA-qB. An unrestricted collinear \
loop measure scales as lambda^D, hence the two base measures give lambda^(2D).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aa062832-0c0b-4c66-84ae-f24151e8ea14"],

Cell["\<\
The dependent momentum qC must simultaneously remain collinear to p5. The two \
independent longitudinal variations delta xiA and delta xiB are confined by \
the in-plane and conjugate light-cone projections, with widths O(lambda) and \
O(lambda^2), respectively. The wide-angle Jacobian is nonzero. Consequently\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7041eaa0-5bd9-4c6b-84ca-6eb15c6416d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["J", "5"], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u5", ".", "p1"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"v5", ".", "p2"}]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v5", ".", "p1"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"u5", ".", "p2"}]}]}]}], "\[And]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u5", ".", "p1"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"v5", ".", "p2"}]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v5", ".", "p1"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"u5", ".", "p2"}]}]}], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"d9b098ee-7fe8-4c32-aa9a-\
578b2b208062"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"scalesAs", "(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "xiA"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "xiB"}]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "3"]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"55f73c97-fdd6-4c22-b249-\
8b5431cdc39e"],

Cell["\<\
This restricted support is the momentum-space image of the depth of the \
parameter-space cancellation. It is essential: counting two ordinary \
collinear loop measures without it misses lambda^3.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"898aee08-1e6c-4292-8ceb-3d3589fd11da"],

Cell["12. Matching parameter- and momentum-space power counting", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"af79ec7b-a95e-4784-b4f0-2a1b8352b28a"],

Cell["\<\
In parameter space, the three path-scale coordinates contribute lambda^(-6) \
and the three normal coordinates contribute lambda^(-3). The resolved LP \
polynomial has weight -4, so P^(-D/2) contributes lambda^(2D). In momentum \
space, the two collinear loop measures and their restricted longitudinal \
support contribute lambda^(2D+3), while six unit propagators contribute \
lambda^(-12).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8edf61c0-72a2-46ce-820e-36a84c161d9d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"representation\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"measure\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"integrand\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"total\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"parameter space\"\>", "\<\"lambda^(-6) lambda^(-3)\"\>", \
"\<\"P^(-D/2) ~ lambda^(2D)\"\>", "\<\"lambda^(2D-9)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"momentum space\"\>", "\<\"lambda^(2D) lambda^3\"\>", "\<\"six \
propagators ~ lambda^(-12)\"\>", "\<\"lambda^(2D-9)\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"deebb536-2b66-4ce1-af46-c30c4cf0a83e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "D"}], "-", "9"}]],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"bedae8ba-d770-4d26-8cf8-\
f4caad404268"],

Cell["\<\
At D=4-2 epsilon both descriptions give lambda^(-1-4 epsilon). Numerators can \
change the integer power, but equality of the two scalar countings \
independently certifies the translation between parameter and momentum space.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"668bcc3b-d7fd-496e-ab1a-16b0235f67a9"],

Cell["13. Central-soft MRK momentum flow and scalar power", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5a5c7aa3-192c-405f-8c21-27f75ef3488c"],

Cell["\<\
For the representative a=1,b=2 path, the hard-scale-normalized LP vector is \
(-4,-4,-1,-4,-4,-4;1). The associated propagator virtualities and one \
consistent component assignment are:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"adbf434b-b23a-4eb4-b03a-f20e781fb7b6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"edge\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"(q+,q-,q_perp) powers\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"q^2 power\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"x0", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{4, 0, 2}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "4"},
    {"x1", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{4, 0, 2}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "4"},
    {"x2", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{0, 1, 2}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "1"},
    {"x3", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{3, 1, 2}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "4"},
    {"x4", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{4, 0, 2}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "4"},
    {"x5", 
     StyleBox["\<\"{4, 0, 2}\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"], "4"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"0e3ef054-a520-481b-8656-9fe33aef1d3d"],

Cell["\<\
Use r=q0 and ell=q0-q4 in hard-scale-normalized momenta. The q0/q1 poles \
pinch r-plus with width delta^4; q4/q5 pinch ell-plus with width delta^4; and \
q2/q3 pinch ell-minus with width delta. Both transverse widths scale as \
delta^2. Thus r has local widths (4,0,2) and ell has widths (4,1,2). The \
two-loop measure has power 4D+1. The six denominator powers sum to 21, so \
their reciprocals contribute delta^(-21).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12c3c374-bb9b-43bf-bde9-dba36840ce4f"],

Cell["\<\
In parameter space define A=x2-X34hat^(-1) delta^3 x3 and B=x1 x4-x0 x5. The \
generic A weight is -1, and the HRF gap restricts it to weight 0; B has \
weight -8. Four tangential coordinates contribute -16, while the Jacobian \
-1/x0 contributes +4. The parameter measure is therefore delta^(-20), while \
the resolved LP polynomial of weight -8 contributes delta^(4D).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3854c540-8315-4010-8e0c-66b1b8122881"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"representation\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"measure\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"integrand\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"total\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"parameter space\"\>", "\<\"delta^(-20)\"\>", "\<\"P^(-D/2) ~ \
delta^(4D)\"\>", "\<\"delta^(4D-20)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"momentum space\"\>", "\<\"delta^(4D+1)\"\>", "\<\"1/Product(q_e^2) \
~ delta^(-21)\"\>", "\<\"delta^(4D-20)\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"85c20f3b-cfae-4971-ad56-34d31e966fb1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[ImaginaryI]", "CS", "scalar"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "D"}], "-", "20"}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"8", " ", "epsilon"}]}], "-", "4"}]]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b1671bac-dca2-4e7f-8492-\
a78eaaf6c759"],

Cell["\<\
This is the dimensionless integral with s12 factored out, which is the \
convention relevant for identifying an infrared region. Restoring the \
engineering-dimension factor s12^(D-6), with s12~delta^(-4), gives an \
additional overall delta^(-4D+24); this trivial conversion should not be \
confused with the HRF region vector.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c99fb8b-6035-430d-8853-dca95ef3f15f"],

Cell["14. Conclusions and scope", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"68de08b7-2fb4-4b02-a638-fc7a29889d1f"],

Cell["\<\
The exactly on-shell near-planar Landshoff region has a positive Landau \
solution on Gamma5=0, three independent normal equations, the pair-product \
generator ideal, hierarchy gap two, and matching scalar power lambda^(-1-4 \
epsilon) in parameter and momentum space. The central-soft MRK degeneration \
has a two-factor ideal, requires asymptotic-order alignment, and has the \
distinct hard-scale-normalized vector (-4,-4,-1,-4,-4,-4;1) and scalar power \
delta^(-4-8 epsilon). The two regions are related through the same \
path-normal geometry and the same unlabeled seed topology, but they are \
physically different regions in different expansions.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"958ac21e-adb8-459a-8988-51fb771cb18f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Appendix: implementation chart and complete exact expressions\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"aac3e55d-7b81-43cd-b281-d36e61b3cba7"],

Cell["\<\
These commands expose the invariant construction and the executable \
near-planar certificate. The audit retains an older off-shell calculation \
internally as a regression reference, but it is not part of the notebook's \
physical definition.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d960add1-23b1-4506-a043-f24e1c2cc02e"],

